alf, m)\n\nmaximum = 0\nfor left_val in left_mod_sums:\n    complement = m - left_val\n    insertion = bisect.bisect_left(right_mod_sums, complement)\n    if insertion > 0:\n        combined = left_val + right_mod_sums[insertion - 1]\n        if combined > maximum:\n            maximum = combined\n\nprint(maximum)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport bisect\n\nn, m = [int(i) for i in input().split()]\narr = [int(i) for i in input().split()]\n\nsplit_point = n // 2\nfirst_half = arr[:split_point]\nsecond_half = arr[split_point:]\n\ndef compute_mod_sums(subarr, modulus):\n    out = []\n    num_elements = len(subarr)\n    for state in range(2 ** num_elements):\n        subtotal = 0\n        for bit_pos in range(num_elements):\n            if state >> bit_pos & 1:\n                subtotal += subarr[bit_pos]\n        out.append(subtotal % modulus)\n    return sorted(out)\n\nleft_mod_sums = compute_mod_sums(first_half, m)\nright_mod_sums = compute_mod_sums(second_half, m)\n\nmaximum = 0\nfor left_val in left_mod_sums:\n    # We want to maximize (left_val + right_val) % m\n    # Since left_val and right_val are both in [0, m-1],\n    # the maximum possible sum is 2*(m-1), but we want the modulo m value\n    # The best case is when left_val + right_val >= m, then (left_val + right_val) % m = left_val + right_val - m\n    # But we want to maximize the modulo value, so we want left_val + right_val to be as close to m-1 as possible\n    # or as close to 2m-1 as possible (which gives m-1 after modulo)\n    # Actually, the maximum modulo value is m-1, so let's try to achieve that\n    # For a given left_val, we want right_val such that (left_val + right_val) % m is maximized\n    # This happens when right_val is as close as possible to (m - 1 - left_val) or (2*m - 1 - left_val)\n    # But since right_val is in [0, m-1], the best is to find right_val such that left_val + right_val is as close to m-1 as possible from below,\n    # or as close to 2m-1 as possible from below (which gives m-1)\n    \n    # Actually, the maximum value of (left_val + right_val) % m is:\n    # - If there exists right_val such that left_val + right_val >= m, then the best is to get as close to 2m-1 as possible, giving m-1\n    # - Otherwise, get as close to m-1 as possible\n    \n    # To maximize (left_val + right_val) % m, we want:\n    # 1. If possible, find right_val such that left_val + right_val >= m and left_val + right_val is as large as possible (but < 2m)\n    #    This gives (left_val + right_val) % m = left_val + right_val - m, which is maximized when left_val + right_val is maximized\n    # 2. Or find right_val such that left_val + right_val < m and is as close to m-1 as possible\n    \n    # For case 1: we want right_val >= m - left_val, and as large as possible\n    # For case 2: we want right_val <= m - 1 - left_val, and as large as possible\n    \n    # Let's find the largest right_val that is <= (m - 1 - left_val)\n    idx = bisect.bisect_right(right_mod_sums, m - 1 - left_val)\n    if idx > 0:\n        candidate1 = left_val + right_mod_sums[idx - 1]\n        if candidate1 > maximum:\n            maximum = candidate1\n    \n    # Find the largest right_val overall (which would give the largest sum when left_val + right_val >= m)\n    if right_mod_sums:\n        # The largest right_val\n        largest_right = right_mod_sums[-1]\n        if left_val + largest_right >= m:\n            candidate2 = (left_val + largest_right) % m\n            if candidate2 > maximum:\n                maximum = candidate2\n        else:\n            # If even the largest right_val doesn't make the sum >= m, then we already considered all possibilities above\n            pass\n\nprint(maximum)\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.768370445162873e-07, -2.0146166207268834e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, 0